			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3646661">
									

<p>I like the idea of the journal entries, to a degree. The whole descent into madness by the hotel director feels earnest and believable (if a bit hamfisted at the end with the whole &quot;preservation of dignity&quot; deal), and all told this feels like something out of a Fallout game. I thoroughly enjoyed that portion of the article. That's the good.</p>
<p>The bad is the anomalous generator. I'm feeling like there's a serious disconnect between a generator that just provides enough power for anything that's hooked up to it and BOOM! Hotel on the motherf**kin moon!</p>
<p>The concepts don't flow well into each other at all and completely jar me out of the whole &quot;Did they piss off the alien mafia?!&quot; deal I was enjoying up until that point. My advice would be to lose the generator completely or find some way to bridge that gap between the anomaly and the effect. Because right now they feel like two separate stories that are competing for my attention while I read this</p>

							</div>

								
					
