<p>When in doubt, do a little and do it well. The idea of a hotel spontaneously ending up on the moon and the journals detailing the final days of the people left in it were done perfectly. If I had to give a reason for why it's up there (and believe me, you absolutely don't have to. The core idea feels strong enough to work on its own)&#8230; I'd make it fit with the Vegas of that time period. Maybe a type green was performing as a magician and made the hotel disappear without any solid plan to bring it back. Maybe the alien mafia got irritated and chose to repossess their property&#8230; then decided it was too much hassle to keep the casino so they dropped it back off in more or less the right area. It doesn't necessarily have to be corny and over the top, it also doesn't have to NOT be corny and over the top, either, it just has to mesh well with what's already established in the rest of the article.</p>

