					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1722371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607373847" alt="Shaggydredlocks" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1722371)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;" >Shaggydredlocks</a></span> <span class="odate time_1512630071 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Dec 2017 07:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3647368">
									

<p>If I were to rework this, I'd retool the article by focusing on the SCPF piecing together everything as they record it.:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So, say, first addendum would be a recording of the state and nature of all the bodies they find, and allowing the events to be inferred from that.</p>
<ul>
<li>Several people found outside the atmospheric safe-zone, with small details that suggest what they were up to/how they attempted to escape.</li>
<li>Cannibalized or mutilated remains in the game area</li>
<li>Some poor sod that locked themselves up in the vault and died alone</li>
<li>Someone of importance strung up and brutalized or crucified</li>
<li>Some of the hired goons something something they ded</li>
</ul>
<p>etc. etc. etc. Basically, think about the arrangement of these things, or other small details about the hotel itself, that build an outline juuust around the happenings therein. A gentle push in the right direction would be more effective (to me) than a hard shove.</p>
<p>Flowing from that, I would maybe follow that with more disparate logs: crude graffiti scrawled in a certain area, a snippet of an account from someone who can only imagine what's actually going on, a suicide note from a gambler&#8230;hell, even some of the diary you've got right now might work out just fine. But again, building around rather than filling completely in.</p>
<p>For -1? I'm not entirely sure what to do with that. <em>Something</em> can come from it, or rather, it can have a place, I suppose, but involving Stock Bad Guis I feel was a poor choice.</p>
<p>Point is, you don't really <em>need</em> it, unless I suppose you need it to be there just to kill everyone else off (it's just a plot point). If that's the case, I'd say it's interchangeable, and I'm certain with some brainstorming you could find something more evocative or alluring or simply just Dark that could serve just as well in that capacity.</p>
</div>
</div>
